#### Problem 3: Load Spikes Overwhelm Services

Peak traffic periods without buffering cause service degradation or complete failures.

**Example Scenario**: Open Enrollment Overload

```csharp
// Member enrollment service without load leveling
public class MemberEnrollmentService
{
    public async Task<EnrollmentResult> EnrollMemberAsync(EnrollmentRequest request)
    {
        // Validate eligibility
        var eligibility = await _eligibilityService.ValidateAsync(request.MemberId);

        // Calculate premium
        var premium = await _premiumService.CalculatePremiumAsync(request);

        // Assign health plan
        var assignment = await _planAssignmentService.AssignPlanAsync(request);

        // Generate ID card
        var idCard = await _idCardService.GenerateCardAsync(request);

        // Send notifications
        await _notificationService.SendEnrollmentConfirmationAsync(request);

        // All steps must complete synchronously
        // During peak load, service becomes overloaded
        return EnrollmentResult.Success(assignment, idCard);
    }
}
```

**2024 Open Enrollment Crisis**:
- State marketplace open enrollment: 30-day window for 2M+ member plan selections
- Final 72 hours: 600K enrollment submissions (10x normal daily volume)
- Enrollment service overwhelmed: CPU 98%, memory exhausted, response times 2-5 minutes
- Cascading failures: eligibility service, premium calculation, ID card generation all degraded
- Impact: 45,000 enrollment failures; members unable to select health plans before deadline
- Emergency response: Throttling at gateway (rejected 30% of requests), extended enrollment period
- Cost: $2.1M in emergency infrastructure scaling, state contract penalties, customer service overflow

